    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me verify the specific fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### Issue 1: Missing named exports in finetune module\n**Problem:** The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./finetune/index.js`, but it was only available through the default export.\n\n**Fix:** Added named exports for the constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) while keeping the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n### Issue 2: Incorrect toxicityMetric signature\n**Problem:** The `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but was called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging harmless words.\n\n**Fix:** Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the interface expected by `runEvaluations`, accepting references as the second parameter but using the default banned terms.\n\n### Verification\n- \u2705 All 28 frai-core tests pass\n- \u2705 All 11 frai-gate tests pass  \n- \u2705 All builds succeed with no errors\n- \u2705 Public API remains intact (constants available through namespace exports)",
